{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/889312-what-is-the-purpose-of-lodges","id":889312,"title":"What is the purpose of Lodges","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-12T13:21:09-07:00","id":889312,"title":"What is the purpose of Lodges","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> What's the in game purpose for having lodges? They feel to me to be really tacked on, just to have a Z axis for the splat, with no real reasoning of it. Shouldn't they just be specialized packs, or if those get too big small protectorates of packs under a common banner? As is now... they just don't mesh with me after reading all the things about how Pack is above all else, and after looking at the Social bonuses/penalties for non pack members, which makes this even less believable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T13:26:22-07:00","id":889319,"title":"","content":"So my first question is, are you asking this having read the new Lodge stuff in The Pack or just what's in the corebook?<br /> <br /> Also:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/889312-what-is-the-purpose-of-lodges#post889312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">after looking at the Social bonuses/penalties for non pack members</div> </div> </div> </div>What's this a reference to? I can't recall social penalties for dealing with non-pack members off-hand, though this may just be my memory being faulty.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T13:50:51-07:00","id":889337,"title":"","content":"@op Have your read the Pack yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T13:52:37-07:00","id":889339,"title":"","content":"Yes, this is after reading the Pack. Corebook doesn't really have much on lodges. <br /> <br /> As for social bonuses, it's in The Pack. Within your own pack you get social bonuses, and anyone outside your pack get's social penalties towards you, so suddenly having a second out of pack grouping (after Tribe) seems a lot less feasible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T14:13:40-07:00","id":889349,"title":"","content":"The big difference between Protectorates and Lodges - esp. from a &quot;game&quot; perspective in terms of their purpose - is that Protectorates are location focused, and Lodges are spiritually focused.<br /> <br /> Protectorates are when the local packs realize they can't handle things divided. They're inherently products of necessity. As such, they provide additional/advanced options for the local werewolf political landscape. The default of &quot;every pack has their own territory and they keep separate from each other baring skirmishes and disputes,&quot; don't really have much if you want inter-pack dealings. Adding Protectorates adds a layer on top of packs that is locally focused and creates ways for conflict and struggle between packs beyond the default.<br /> <br /> Lodges are when groups of werewolves realize they have a goal beyond that of pack or Tribe, and dedicate themselves to it. This creates groups with much tighter cultures that can span territories and Protectorates. For the game this provides a few things. First, as Protectorates expands on the local political layers of the game, the Lodges expand on the spiritual layers of the game. They provide more spiritual directives pulling adherents in more directions. Second, they create a new source of dramatic conflict. The Tribes are loose philosophies that are easily adapted, allowing packs to reach compromise between members of different Tribes among their ranks. Adherents have very strong philosophies that they can't compromise for the sake of their pack. This adds to the game a way to have intra-pack conflicts that are easier on players that don't like having PC groups full of people that just don't get along. The non-Lodge members of a pack can value the strength and skill an adherent brings to the table - as this aids instead of compromising the pack's ideals - while providing conflict over the risk of divided loyalties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T15:03:37-07:00","id":889381,"title":"","content":"One of the big things I thought they managed was to show the different perspectives werewolves can take. It's easy to skim the Forsaken book and just see it as Forsaken versus the Pure, but there's a wide variety in between. This offers opportunities for players who, for some reason or another, don't want to play the existing tribes exactly as written. They can have their characters be more attuned to their lodge, instead. The lodges allow writers and Storytellers options to really focus on existing aspects of werewolf lodges or auspices, or deviate from them entirely into something new, similar to the Eaters of the Dead or Temple of Helios.<br /> <br /> Plus it really helps to get across the strangeness of the spirit, and how strange it is to be a werewolf. As the first two chapters have gotten across, being a werewolf is weird, and only other werewolves will really know what it's like. It's easy for people like that to fall into spiritual traps and strange cult-like behavior, considering the things that fulfill them. There's aspects of the Hisil that want to take advantage of this, and sometimes 'just' driven werewolves who manage to find something that appeals to their own personal realm of weirdness. It's easy for us to look at the Temple of Helios and think they're crazy, but I think it's easy to imagine a freshly Changed werewolf having bad experiences with the tribes and their warring falling in with something like the Temple, which can balance their soul and give them direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T15:08:54-07:00","id":889385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/889312-what-is-the-purpose-of-lodges?p=889339#post889339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, this is after reading the Pack. Corebook doesn't really have much on lodges.<br /> <br /> As for social bonuses, it's in The Pack. Within your own pack you get social bonuses, and anyone outside your pack get's social penalties towards you, so suddenly having a second out of pack grouping (after Tribe) seems a lot less feasible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you get us a citation, because I'm also curious. The only thing I've seen so far like that is the &quot;Like-Minded/Us Against The World&quot; thing on page 63, but that's not really a social penalty for dealing with outsiders as much as it is a bulwark against outside influence. You might not have that instinctual amount of trust that you do with packmates, but that doesn't mean you can't deal with and have rewarding social relationships outside of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T15:22:37-07:00","id":889393,"title":"","content":"Griatus may have been thinking of page 63, talking about totems and the bonuses and advantages of sharing a totem. 'If a pack member uses Social maneuvering against a packmate,her first impression is considered to be one step higher than normal, and her target has one fewer Door than normal...Non-packmates attempting Social maneuvers against the pack have their first impression downgraded by one step, and the pack member has one additional Door.' Which I don't think means what he thinks it means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T16:23:14-07:00","id":889434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/889312-what-is-the-purpose-of-lodges?p=889393#post889393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Griatus may have been thinking of page 63, talking about totems and the bonuses and advantages of sharing a totem. 'If a pack member uses Social maneuvering against a packmate,her first impression is considered to be one step higher than normal, and her target has one fewer Door than normal...Non-packmates attempting Social maneuvers against the pack have their first impression downgraded by one step, and the pack member has one additional Door.' Which I don't think means what he thinks it means.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's hardly a penalty, yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T23:02:08-07:00","id":889679,"title":"","content":"Most people have a personal life around their home, a work life around the office, and a hobby-driven life around something else, like church or swing dancing.<br /> <br /> Pack, Tribe, Lodge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T00:52:22-07:00","id":889730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/889312-what-is-the-purpose-of-lodges?p=889393#post889393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Griatus may have been thinking of page 63, talking about totems and the bonuses and advantages of sharing a totem. 'If a pack member uses Social maneuvering against a packmate,her first impression is considered to be one step higher than normal, and her target has one fewer Door than normal...Non-packmates attempting Social maneuvers against the pack have their first impression downgraded by one step, and the pack member has one additional Door.' Which I don't think means what he thinks it means.</div> </div> </div> </div>That mechanic is intended to simulate confirmation bias and reinforce that it's easier to get like minded people (your pack) to agree with you, and harder for outside views (not pack) to change your mind. It doesn't penalise pack mates dealing with outsiders, or outsiders dealing with pack mates, except if they specifically attempt Social manoeuvring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T03:17:56-07:00","id":889768,"title":"","content":"I think of Lodges as mini-Tribes. In many ways, Tribes are like individual &quot;religions&quot; - philosophies and teachings and commandments you follow. So, a Lodge would be joining a more focused part of religion, or perhaps a Local flavor of such. Its like having a Russian Orthodox, Catholic, Baptist churches all within a few blocks as well as a church that combines a bit of Buddhist teachings. They are all Christian, but there is a different focus in each, you'll find different denominations around the world. Or cults that challlenge mainstream religions. And so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T03:47:31-07:00","id":889779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/889312-what-is-the-purpose-of-lodges?p=889730#post889730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That mechanic is intended to simulate confirmation bias and reinforce that it's easier to get like minded people (your pack) to agree with you, and harder for outside views (not pack) to change your mind. It doesn't penalise pack mates dealing with outsiders, or outsiders dealing with pack mates, except if they specifically attempt Social manoeuvring.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Since the Social Maneuvering System is meant to replace normal social actions - yes, it sorta does. Also, mechanics are there to tell something about the world - and now by default, with everyone else you have worse relationships, you need longer and more time to get them to do things for you. And remember, the bulwark works both ways - while yes, it's harder for them to approach you, it's also harder for you to approach them (other werewolves) because they are members of a different pack. <br /> <br /> Alright, I still don't get how did Lodges came to be, and why wouldn't Lodges be a pack, or a group of packs. Why wouldn't you join up with people of your own lodge in packs? The only thing which comes to my mind is &quot;more choices for PCs&quot;. But in Universe, when you're joining a Lodge, why wouldn't you go for it's pack? Or with how strongly the pack is emphasised, why would you join a religion when you already have one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T04:13:06-07:00","id":889788,"title":"","content":"With regards to Lodges and Tribes, it really comes down to which denomination of a religion you ascribe to. You follow Destroyer Wolf at its core because you believe Werewolves are the greatest prey and you follow the ethos of Offer No Surrender You Would Not Accept. But Lodges are a distillation or a deviation of that core concept. Tribal Pillars are specifically a group under the umbrella of the wider faith that hinges on a single facet that you join up with. You still relate to other Blood Talons, but you know the Garmir have the best mindset for you. <br /> <br /> Its like growing up as a Christian and not really diving in too deeply, but as you grow up and look around you find you really jive with Protestants, or Catholics, or Baptists, or etc. Its not like you didn't believe in Christ beforehand, but you didn't have a specific viewpoint of how that faith should be practiced until you joined a specific group.<br /> <br /> Packs based around a single Lodges are completely fine in setting and do happen according to the fluff. But they aren't the only way because, just like real life, people of various faiths and religions work, live, and love together all the time. <br /> <br /> That Packs are instinctively defensive against outsiders, especially other werewolves, fits pretty well that they have an additional Door people have to break through to get to them. The fluff in both editions heavily plays on how hard it is for them to work together, and the mechanics backing that up to a degree makes sense. You can come to them with the best of intentions and respect, and they can listen to you, but at the end of it all they still are working with a mindset that you're an outsider looking to fuck up what they have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T04:30:37-07:00","id":889794,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar294_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"294\" data-vbnamecard=\"294\">Griautis</a> social maneuvering is meant to simulate long-term social conditioning. Standard social actions, such as instant Strength+Intimidation rolls are still valid and unaffected.<br /> <br /> Regarding Lodges? They're cults. Not everyond is going to join the same. And they are specializations. What is so hard to grasp from them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T05:07:16-07:00","id":889798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/889312-what-is-the-purpose-of-lodges?p=889779#post889779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the Social Maneuvering System is meant to replace normal social actions - yes, it sorta does. Also, mechanics are there to tell something about the world - and now by default, with everyone else you have worse relationships, you need longer and more time to get them to do things for you. And remember, the bulwark works both ways - while yes, it's harder for them to approach you, it's also harder for you to approach them (other werewolves) because they are members of a different pack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ephsy got this one. The Social Maneuvering System isn't meant to replace normal social actions, it's to give certain kinds of social actions more depth and is used 'for applying persuasion and social pressure over time.' It's harder to get a werewolf to change via social pressure because they're part of a pack that accepts them, and a bit harder to persuade them to do things they wouldn't ordinarily be willing to do. An extra door is not exactly a social dead end, either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alright, I still don't get how did Lodges came to be, and why wouldn't Lodges be a pack, or a group of packs. Why wouldn't you join up with people of your own lodge in packs? The only thing which comes to my mind is &quot;more choices for PCs&quot;. But in Universe, when you're joining a Lodge, why wouldn't you go for it's pack? Or with how strongly the pack is emphasised, why would you join a religion when you already have one? </div> </div> </div>There's a lot of lodges where you would be in packs with other members of the lodge. A member of the Temple of Apollo is not likely to be teaming up with an Iron Master and a Ivory Claw. But not all lodges are as rigid as you seem to think. The Thousand Steel Teeth are gearheads, they don't require you to be among others of the same pack, and their devotionals are not restrictive or going to go against the ideas in other tribes. A member of one of the pillar lodges is an exemplary member of a certain tribe. There's nothing restrictive about that unless other packmembers really had something against your beliefs, which again may come up with some lodges but there's no reason to believe it would come up in all of them.<br /> <br /> The pack isn't a religion, it's family. Some families may demand you share the same religion as them, but that's not universal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-13-2016, 08:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T08:22:46-07:00","id":890574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/889312-what-is-the-purpose-of-lodges?p=889779#post889779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And remember, the bulwark works both ways - while yes, it's harder for them to approach you, it's also harder for you to approach them (other werewolves) because they are members of a different pack.</div> </div> </div> </div>This indeed make interpacks relationships more difficult. But it's important to note that it doesn't apply to relationships with people outside of packs. Your friend that's outside the pack may have trouble changing your mind but you won't have any more difficulty changing his than before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T19:18:22-07:00","id":890916,"title":"","content":"One could read lodges as being similar to camps from werewolf the apocalypse, albeit a smidge more flexible. But then everything in chronicles of darkness is more flexible then classic. Hell comparing the Fenrir to the Blood Talons might point that one out. &gt;.&gt; I'd argue the most flexible thing about classic would be the black spirals and even they're pretty set in stone as to what they're about. <br /> <br /> So yes, lodges serve the purpose of being directed social groups. So you've got tribe &gt; hunting purpose; lodge &gt; specified stylistic hunting purpose that fits personal belief systems; packs &gt; family you hunt with. The thing with all of that is you don't need to join any of em, life is just a smidge easier with all your bases covered.<br /> <br /> To use an extreme example lets look at Odinistic Skin heads. So they worship a form of Old Norse religion. All well and good, but likely they also belong to some manner of local close knit group that is like minded. Maybe the soldier of Odin out of Finland? And even closer you have your individual gangs/groups at the ground level that act as your pack/family. That's a way to relate it. Course there's other examples, that one just happens to be easier to throw out there with the cut boundary lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T20:29:34-07:00","id":890947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/889312-what-is-the-purpose-of-lodges?p=890574#post890574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This indeed make interpacks relationships more difficult. But it's important to note that it doesn't apply to relationships with people outside of packs. Your friend that's outside the pack may have trouble changing your mind but you won't have any more difficulty changing his than before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. But also be aware of the danger of the enemy within. Your friend may have greater difficulty swaying you to his way of thinking, but if he can manage it, he can use your insider influence to spread the idea like wild fire. <br /> <br /> Packs (and other predators) that hunt through social means study their enemy closely, identifying the weak link, and use this opening to spread disunity through lies and misinformation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}